{"agent_id":"pp3g-6NK3-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:47:02.540268859Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"58e2822d-bb12-4641-a2e7-a93a78918225","author":"pp3g-6NK3-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"Independent review — findings (WHY / WHAT / HOW-CERTAIN / WHAT-NOT-TESTED embedded per item):\n\n1. {statement: A shared log line's run identifier is not yet a proven agent identity; the proposal leaves attribution mapping undefined. | why-it-matters: A stale/restarted process or multiple sessions can be assigned another agent's request/error, causing the wrong investigation or destructive action. The shipped logger emits run=<runID>, not an agent/worktree/issue identity (fork/opencode-src/packages/core/src/observability/logging.ts:49-52). | cheapest-test: Launch two agents, restart one, and interleave concurrent requests; verify every line maps to the correct agent across run-ID changes. | severity: MUST FIX; certainty=evidence-based; what-not-tested=live multi-agent attribution.}\n\n2. {statement: The parser contract is unspecified and must not infer safety-critical state from free-form formatted logs. | why-it-matters: The formatter quotes/escapes values and flattens nested fields (fork/opencode-src/packages/core/src/observability/logging.ts:6-20,44-47); S2 and v2 format differences, multiline causes, or renamed fields can turn parked, healthy, and dead into the same classification. Parser failure must be UNKNOWN/do-not-kill, not a guessed verdict. | cheapest-test: Fixture-test every known S2/v2 success, retry, error, completion, multiline, malformed, and schema-version line; assert fail-closed behavior. | severity: MUST FIX; certainty=evidence-based; what-not-tested=actual v2 runtime output.}\n\n3. {statement: Rotation/truncation recovery is absent from the proposal's operational contract. | why-it-matters: tail -F-style behavior can miss lines, replay duplicates, or reset state on rename, copytruncate, or startup; an event gap is exactly the failure class the design claims to reduce. | cheapest-test: Exercise rename-create, copytruncate, deletion/recreation, partial-line writes, and watcher restart while asserting monotonic cursor coverage and deduplicated events. | severity: MUST FIX; certainty=guess; what-not-tested=implementation because none is supplied.}\n\n4. {statement: The 60-second poll is not demonstrably an independent watcher-health backstop. | why-it-matters: The existing loop itself performs periodic polling and posts only selected verdict transitions (scripts/liveness-watchdog.sh:147-191); if the new tailer and its supervisor share a process, host, log path, or failure domain, both can fail silently. A claimed backstop needs an externally observed heartbeat and an alert when the tailer is stale. | cheapest-test: Kill/freeze the tailer, corrupt its input, and block Crosslink while leaving the poller running; verify an independent health signal and recovery alert. | severity: MUST FIX; certainty=evidence-based; what-not-tested=systemd deployment.}\n\n5. {statement: Automatic spiral kill has no explicit ownership, authorization, race, or target-integrity protocol. | why-it-matters: Between evidence collection and kill, the session may recover, the tmux name may be reused, or the process may be a shell/orchestrator rather than the intended agent. Existing watchdog policy is monitor/notify only and explicitly has no kill/relaunch (agent-orchestration-playbook.md:551-557,576-586). | cheapest-test: Use a test harness with PID/session reuse, recovery during confirmation, watcher restart, and concurrent operator action; require a signed/expiring opt-in, exact PID/start-time validation, dry-run, grace period, and durable kill receipt. | severity: MUST FIX; certainty=evidence-based; what-not-tested=operator-granted authority semantics.}\n\n6. {statement: High repetition plus no commit/checkpoint is not a sufficiently discriminating definition of a spiral. | why-it-matters: Legitimate polling, compiler/test retries, repeated tool output, long reasoning, and a blocked Crosslink can all satisfy both predicates; the existing methodology explicitly treats process liveness and meaningful progress as different (docs/research/Workflow Topology Design and Reasoning Record.md:331-334; to-file/EDASES Execution Engine reviews.md:726). Auto-kill can discard valid work. | cheapest-test: Replay labeled traces for slow reasoning, repeated tests, retry backoff, verbose generation, Crosslink outage, true loop, and stream death; measure false-kill rate before enabling destructive action. | severity: MUST FIX; certainty=evidence-based; what-not-tested=the proposed similarity algorithm and threshold.}\n\n7. {statement: Evidence tails may contain prompts, paths, provider causes, or credentials and cannot be posted verbatim by default. | why-it-matters: The logger serializes arbitrary causes/annotations (fork/opencode-src/packages/core/src/observability/logging.ts:13-20); attaching ~30 lines to Crosslink expands the disclosure boundary and persists secrets. | cheapest-test: Seed logs with representative API errors, environment-like values, prompts, and paths; verify deterministic redaction before comment creation and bounded size. | severity: MUST FIX; certainty=evidence-based; what-not-tested=production log sensitivity.}\n\n8. {statement: Unresolved-request aging lacks a correlation and deadline model. | why-it-matters: Concurrent requests, retries, sparse legitimate chunks, and a response logged in a different shape can leave a request apparently unresolved; the existing documented per-chunk timeout is 5 minutes (model-discipline.md:254-267), so an arbitrary monitor threshold can contradict runtime behavior. | cheapest-test: Correlate request start/end/error IDs under concurrent requests and replay inter-chunk gaps around the configured timeout; require UNKNOWN when correlation is incomplete. | severity: SHOULD CONSIDER; certainty=evidence-based; what-not-tested=actual request event vocabulary.}\n\n9. {statement: The event stream and transition-comment path need bounded resource/backpressure behavior. | why-it-matters: Per-agent trailing windows, high-volume logs, pane evidence, and Crosslink comment retries can grow memory or generate an alert storm; the current implementation has one comment per action and no backoff/circuit breaker (scripts/liveness-watchdog.sh:169-189). | cheapest-test: Stress with many agents and synthetic high-rate logs while making Crosslink slow/unavailable; assert bounded memory, disk, queue, and deduplicated/coalesced alerts. | severity: SHOULD CONSIDER; certainty=guess; what-not-tested=scale envelope.}\n\nVerdict: MODIFY. Do not adopt the proposal as written. The log is valuable corroborating evidence and can improve diagnosis, but first ship a fail-closed, schema-versioned attribution/parser and rotation-tested tailer, independently supervised health path, redaction, and a non-destructive candidate state. Keep spiral detection operator-confirmed until replay testing establishes a low false-kill rate and the exact kill authority/target protocol is implemented and tested. Rationale: the motivating incident supports adding log evidence, not the stronger inference that free-form shared-log classifications are safe to act on.","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:47:02.533915073Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:Qz3te/SlYhdAXvqN++pkBuFIMi/Ih3KPYJAFtLwDtH0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgRP2JBy6xVmSg1ID2I+OIA8m+TsgPc5KXL0JOKTpfm4UAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAPugYTXbOyweJNngcZHF9KFFFHIlOQzBWYBL/5JodkYP783kGPxQ2B6pYPOEW8NukSWUJqHbMQ8BxXF2TrtKqBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Qz3te/SlYhdAXvqN++pkBuFIMi/Ih3KPYJAFtLwDtH0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgRP2JBy6xVmSg1ID2I+OIA8m+TsgPc5KXL0JOKTpfm4UAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO0PrX0uBzWdeN7QkD3n1M080Hm+8oDZQ0WyApVwT30SryYgTwjkkmyFdHIW1RYa+8TI0NCwDpborj1vqwB0fQA="}
